[Music]  a new lawsuit accuses tech giant google  of racial bias against its black workers  april curley a former google employee  claims in her lawsuit that the company  steered black hires toward lower paying  jobs using their knowledge while denying  them chances to advance she says that  she was fired after she spoke out lilia  luciano spoke to curley about her  experience working for google  it was my dream job that dream for april  curly who joined google in 2014 meant  leading the change she wished to see in  big tech  my role was to  engage with historically black colleges  and universities and recruit some of the  brightest  most talented black students and she did  i brought over 500 talented qualified  students to google to be hired but in a  lawsuit she filed against google she  claims she and those student recruits  were pigeon-holed into dead-end jobs  received lower pay and were often  dismissed as being not googly enough  what were they saying it is a fit test  and it is to see if  the wording normally is would you grab a  beer with that person it's a very unfair  metric she claims in the suit that she  and other black employees endured micro  and macro aggressions  i was told that i was intimidating  and that i was never tapped for  leadership  opportunities because my white managers  said that they were afraid of me curly  says after she complained about her  treatment she was put on a performance  review and ultimately lost her job  cbs legal analyst ricky clemen  what should be most concerning to google  about  what this case lays out the worst fact  for google on the face of the complaint  is that they terminated her after she  raised issues of racial discrimination  so it looks like it's retaliatory  civil rights attorney ben crump is  representing curly in the lawsuit google  has been referred to as one of the  greatest disruptors  in the past century where it's not  enough to disrupt technology if you  don't also disrupt racism and  discrimination  beyond the lawsuit reuters reported that  california's department of fair  employment and housing last year  launched its own investigation into the  company's treatment of black women in  response google said they would  investigate any concerns to make sure  our workplace is representative and  equitable  in the wake of the social justice  protests of 2020 google launched a  multi-million dollar initiative to hire  more black workers google didn't respond  to a request for comment but it told the  washington post in the past it doesn't  agree with curly's description of her  termination the company's annual  diversity report shows the number of  black employees hired went from 5.5 in  2020 to 8.8  last year but curly says representation  isn't just about hiring it's about  retention  and what does it do not having people of  color in the room it violates their core  value number one  to work with great people  well great people include black and  brown people  for cbs mornings lilia luciano san  francisco  so quite a story there quite a lawsuit  there may be more to it so reuters and  exclusive back in december spoke to  seven current and former black employees  female at google who all felt  marginalized  the turnover rate is higher than other  groups and as lilia mentioned the civil  rights regulator there in california is  investigating so things may be happening

